      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Ten new pentangular polyphenols, namely amexanthomycins A-J (1-10) were isolated from the strain Amycolatopsis mediterranei S699∆rifA constructed by deleting the polyketide synthase genes responsible for the biosynthesis of rifamycins. Their structures were elucidated on the basis of 1D and 2D NMR spectroscopic data and high-resolution ESIMS. Amexanthomycins A-C (1-3) showed inhibitory activity against human DNA topoisomerases."},
